# CORE manifest of the ignore rules the framework itself needs.
#
# This file always updates; `.gitignore` does not (it is `_skip_if_exists`, because a
# consumer inevitably adds rules of their own and `copier update` would otherwise revert
# them wholesale on every sync — which is exactly what v0.16.0 did to a live consumer,
# silently removing its `.env` rule among others).
#
# The sync drivers diff a consumer’s `.gitignore` against this list and REPORT missing
# framework rules. They do not apply them: a consumer may have deleted a rule deliberately,
# and re-adding it behind their back is how an observer goes blind (a run-record ignore rule
# re-introduced by an update once hid exactly the files a detector was looking for).
.claude/.current-task
.claude/.paused-tasks
.claude/.last-update-check
.claude/scratchpad.md
.claude/scheduled-processes.json
.claude/settings.local.json
**/scheduled-runs/202[0-9]-*.md
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.claude/debug/
.claude/tmp/
.vscode/

# v0.16.0 (lease protocol): per-clone and per-session identity, plus the local cache of
# back-pointers to claim comments. The authoritative record lives on GitHub, not here, so
# losing this cache is safe: the lease still expires on its TTL and anyone can pick it up.
.claude/.clone-id
.claude/.sessions/
.claude/skills/lease/.state/
